Subject: [PATCH] [mlir] Compute slices from explicit stacks

`getBackwardSliceImpl` calls itself for the defining op of every operand
(and of every value used in the op's regions and defined above them,
unless omitted) and for the parent of a block argument, and
`getForwardSliceImpl` for every op nested in the op's regions and every
user of its results. Each takes a native frame per op on the current
use-def path, so a slice of a long chain of straight-line code overflows
the stack of a thread with a small one; `matchReduction`, which linalg's
vectorizer asks of every reduction, takes such a slice.

Both now keep their path on an explicit stack. Searching changes no IR,
so the values or ops an op leads to are listed when its visit begins and
each is tested against the slice and the path when its turn comes, as
before: the slices hold the same ops in the same order, the filter is
called on the same ops, `visited` is restored as the recursion restored
it, and a value that fails still ends the walk of the region it is used
in.
---
